WEBVTT

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:05.279
Once, when many planets
intermingled and

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.716
the boundary between man
and god was vague...

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:14.221
There was a tale of a particular family.
A tale of love and rebirth.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:27.167
Sometimes I think things over.
It helps to cheer me up.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:37.678
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:44.552
This place has always
meant everything to me.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.857
It rains so beautifully here.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.296
I can dance like the wind.

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:00.801
Even now, I'm having fun.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.640
I have a better sense of
rhythm than you'd think.

00:01:07.141 --> 00:01:12.313
It felt as though every time
I heard a certain someone's voice,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:22.723
I would think back to how
I grew up surrounded by laughter.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:28.762
Yes, anywhere would have
done as a place to call home.

00:01:28.762 --> 00:01:34.301
Farewell, sunshine!
The night rises up invitingly.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:39.573
It's okay, this world moves
in a way that will connect us.

00:01:39.807 --> 00:01:46.280
So that we can all smile
together once again.

00:02:02.296 --> 00:02:04.131
Someone in the employ of the Shrine

00:02:04.665 --> 00:02:08.769
shouldn't speak of destroying
the world so lightly.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:15.075
It's not that I don't care about
the Shrine or the other planes.

00:02:17.878 --> 00:02:21.181
I'm just wondering if there's
some way we can work this out.

00:02:21.715 --> 00:02:26.220
Let's All Think About
What We Can Do

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.688
Chapter 25: The
Present (19)/ Inari A

00:02:32.026 --> 00:02:34.495
| believe you're aware of this,

00:02:34.828 --> 00:02:36.563
but our job at the Shrine

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.633
is to act on behalf of God
to maintain the balance

00:02:39.633 --> 00:02:41.268
Unified Planetary Organization
The Shrine in the planes.

00:02:42.102 --> 00:02:44.204
To keep the living on the twelve planets,

00:02:44.371 --> 00:02:46.106
and the dead outside the barrier.

00:02:46.774 --> 00:02:49.176
This was all decided in the beginning.

00:02:50.277 --> 00:02:53.447
The existence of a 13th planet
violates the laws of the universe.

00:02:53.747 --> 00:02:56.150
It cannot be allowed.

00:02:59.953 --> 00:03:00.821
You were there.

00:03:01.121 --> 00:03:02.623
You heard it.

00:03:03.991 --> 00:03:08.295
Or did you just happen to forget
it as you reincarnated your soul?

00:03:08.762 --> 00:03:10.597
| didn't forget,

00:03:11.598 --> 00:03:13.267
but nobody said anything to me.

00:03:14.668 --> 00:03:16.003
Stop this.

00:03:16.236 --> 00:03:18.238
God's intervention must be avoided.

00:03:18.939 --> 00:03:23.444
Then how did the Looking Glass City
manage to exist for this long?

00:03:24.511 --> 00:03:30.117
If you're right,
and it really shouldn't exist,

00:03:30.684 --> 00:03:34.655
why hasn't it been a
problem before now?

00:03:36.256 --> 00:03:38.792
Neither God nor the Shrine
wants it to exist,

00:03:39.126 --> 00:03:42.896
so how was Sensei able to create it?

00:03:44.231 --> 00:03:48.635
Why am I able to be here with
my mom and everyone else?

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.774
If it's wrong, why is it possible?

00:03:54.975 --> 00:03:57.678
Who decides, when and where,

00:03:57.945 --> 00:04:00.547
if something's allowed or not,
High Priest?

00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:06.253
Just because it's a world that
didn't exist at the start,

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:09.223
and the Shrine doesn't want it,

00:04:10.157 --> 00:04:13.293
| can't agree that this place
shouldn't exist!

00:04:48.896 --> 00:04:51.832
No matter what bad things
happen because of it,

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:54.868
| don't want to pretend
it never existed.

00:04:55.702 --> 00:04:59.072
| don't want to renounce
the world I see.

00:05:01.308 --> 00:05:07.781
| want to know the truth about myself,
and the world I've found.

00:05:18.358 --> 00:05:20.394
Tell me, High Priest.

00:05:21.829 --> 00:05:24.965
If I'm not true to myself here,

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.734
I'm sure I...

00:05:30.604 --> 00:05:31.505
| won't be able...

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.275
...to see anything anymore.

00:05:51.391 --> 00:05:52.025
Koto...

00:05:53.727 --> 00:05:54.461
Koto!

00:05:55.262 --> 00:05:57.698
Koto, you're wonderful!

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:00.167
The most wonderful,

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.603
the most special, the most
blessed miracle of all!

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.673
Sensei... what's gotten into you?

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.675
Listen to me carefully, Koto.

00:06:09.243 --> 00:06:10.577
I'm God.

00:06:15.782 --> 00:06:17.050
What?

00:06:17.951 --> 00:06:19.953
Dad, what do you mean?

00:06:25.225 --> 00:06:27.661
There's something that's
always bothered me.

00:06:28.161 --> 00:06:30.697
When the world was created,
the rules were created, too.

00:06:31.265 --> 00:06:36.003
Back then, there was only me,
the High Priest, and our dad.

00:06:36.436 --> 00:06:39.806
Our dad was a hopelessly lazy man,

00:06:40.207 --> 00:06:42.576
so he hid himself away

00:06:42.943 --> 00:06:46.847
and left me and the High Priest
with a ton of work.

00:06:47.714 --> 00:06:49.149
Honestly, I can't really blame him.

00:06:49.616 --> 00:06:52.386
That's why he created us, after all.

00:06:53.153 --> 00:06:55.422
He's the Creator,
so we'll do what he wants.

00:06:55.889 --> 00:06:58.125
And it's not like there
was anything else to do.

00:06:58.992 --> 00:07:01.561
The High Priest created subcontractors

00:07:01.561 --> 00:07:03.196
to control and unite the worlds.

00:07:03.897 --> 00:07:05.565
| helped him at first.

00:07:05.799 --> 00:07:08.735
It was kind of fun,
and it was a job worth doing.

00:07:09.269 --> 00:07:12.773
This was before it was even
given the name "Shrine."

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.876
There were these
huge lizards back then!

00:07:16.376 --> 00:07:18.045
It was a fun time.

00:07:18.645 --> 00:07:20.113
| liked it.

00:07:21.048 --> 00:07:22.983
But, well, it came to an end.

00:07:23.951 --> 00:07:26.820
The Ice Age came and went,
humans appeared,

00:07:27.254 --> 00:07:30.991
and my older brother and I spent
our days just doing our jobs.

00:07:31.925 --> 00:07:34.895
My brother is a generous and
hardworking man, as you know.

00:07:35.262 --> 00:07:37.264
He did his work faithfully every day,

00:07:37.664 --> 00:07:39.366
but I was a little different.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.802
You know, it was interesting.

00:07:42.002 --> 00:07:43.437
Every now and then,

00:07:43.437 --> 00:07:46.506
the status quo would change
in ways we had nothing to do with.

00:07:47.007 --> 00:07:48.342
Don't you think that's weird?

00:07:48.809 --> 00:07:50.610
We were in charge, but things

00:07:50.911 --> 00:07:53.447
we knew nothing about were
happening on their own.

00:07:54.114 --> 00:07:56.183
If they worked out, that was fine,

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:58.986
but ever since humanity appeared,

00:07:59.152 --> 00:08:01.621
things simply got beyond our control.

00:08:02.489 --> 00:08:05.492
They did whatever they wanted,
and nothing ever worked out.

00:08:06.059 --> 00:08:07.728
It was such a mess that,

00:08:08.028 --> 00:08:12.299
after a while, we didn't even know
what "worked out” meant anymore.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.036
Deep down, it all seemed stupid to me.

00:08:16.603 --> 00:08:18.305
There was no way I was going to

00:08:18.305 --> 00:08:21.875
make everything my responsibility
and keep doing my job,

00:08:22.142 --> 00:08:23.677
like my brother.

00:08:24.478 --> 00:08:28.081
So I decided I would do whatever I wanted.

00:08:29.049 --> 00:08:32.753
With the promise that I'd be there
when he needed my help, of course.

00:08:34.755 --> 00:08:40.060
|I caused some problems, sure,
but I was also pretty helpful, wasn't I?

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:40.761
Brother?

00:08:41.428 --> 00:08:43.830
The High Priest is your brother, Dad?

00:08:45.799 --> 00:08:47.934
You don't usually talk this much.

00:08:48.235 --> 00:08:50.637
How could I keep quiet?

00:08:51.071 --> 00:08:55.342
See, my job from the start
was the creation of life.

00:08:55.642 --> 00:08:59.913
So something being born
from somebody besides me

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.382
was a little bit of an accident.

00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:05.218
At first, I thought it was disgusting.

00:09:05.852 --> 00:09:09.523
| don't really like myself much,
to put it mildly.

00:09:10.023 --> 00:09:16.563
The idea of another me coming out
from another person made me sick.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.332
Someone so close to me,
and yet not me!

00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:23.804
And the rules of life meant that
there was no way to change this.

00:09:24.337 --> 00:09:25.939
It's a tragedy, don't you think?

00:09:26.573 --> 00:09:30.477
"The power to create life"
may sound like a big deal,

00:09:31.044 --> 00:09:34.514
but really, everything
happens as God wills it.

00:09:34.915 --> 00:09:36.850
But once I started raising her,

00:09:37.184 --> 00:09:42.189
she was just so perfect, so smart,
so cute, so wonderful!

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.525
My heart trembled with joy, Koto!

00:09:47.327 --> 00:09:50.597
| decided that if this wonderful girl

00:09:50.831 --> 00:09:53.400
grew up the way I wanted her to,

00:09:53.867 --> 00:09:55.268
| would entrust her

00:09:55.836 --> 00:09:59.873
with the wish that I couldn't
fulfill for myself!

00:10:02.576 --> 00:10:08.548
And now, you've grown beyond
my wildest hopes and dreams!

00:10:09.382 --> 00:10:13.687
Koto, you are the other me that I wanted!

00:10:23.463 --> 00:10:25.966
Reveal the truth of which
the heavens are silent,

00:10:26.466 --> 00:10:28.435
and show me the answer.

00:10:31.037 --> 00:10:33.039
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:10:33.039 --> 00:10:34.508
<i>Chapter 26: The
Present (20)/ nariB</i>

00:10:40.647 --> 00:10:42.949
What are you thinking?

00:10:43.416 --> 00:10:44.751
Just what she said.

00:10:45.585 --> 00:10:49.055
I'll destroy all the planes,
using this place as my base.

00:10:56.196 --> 00:10:56.997
High Priest!

00:10:57.497 --> 00:10:58.298
High Priest!

00:10:58.298 --> 00:10:59.733
Are you okay, High Priest?

00:10:59.966 --> 00:11:02.035
Return to the Shrine.

00:11:02.035 --> 00:11:02.802
But...

00:11:03.069 --> 00:11:04.037
Inari...

00:11:05.839 --> 00:11:06.673
I'm sorry.

00:11:06.873 --> 00:11:10.076
What did you do to her—

00:11:14.581 --> 00:11:16.016
I'm sorry, Koto.

00:11:16.383 --> 00:11:17.684
I'll explain later.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.029
That which shines and so is divine.

00:11:29.629 --> 00:11:34.734
Your light will make a crack
in this twisted world.

00:11:46.313 --> 00:11:49.316
Are you really the priest?

00:11:50.483 --> 00:11:53.286
Were you surprised to find
yourself with a little sister?

00:11:55.956 --> 00:11:58.191
Isn't Koto cute?

00:12:02.729 --> 00:12:04.564
So you haven't come back to us?

00:12:05.966 --> 00:12:08.168
We're not going to
all live here together?

00:12:21.514 --> 00:12:26.152
I've been waiting for you to come back.

00:12:27.487 --> 00:12:28.321
This whole time.

00:12:30.824 --> 00:12:32.592
When you both came back,

00:12:34.094 --> 00:12:38.531
| was going to give you back
the prayer beads, and the name,

00:12:39.499 --> 00:12:44.838
and then we could talk about
old times for a while, and then...

00:12:45.672 --> 00:12:49.676
And then it could all be over.

00:12:52.912 --> 00:12:53.613
But...

00:12:54.114 --> 00:12:57.017
You haven't used them?

00:12:57.384 --> 00:12:59.019
| left them for you.

00:13:01.087 --> 00:13:03.423
| was just holding on to them!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.358
It's always been like that.

00:13:05.692 --> 00:13:08.395
A new life, these beads...

00:13:08.995 --> 00:13:10.530
| didn't want any of it!

00:13:13.233 --> 00:13:16.336
I'm sick of your whims ruling my life!

00:13:17.203 --> 00:13:21.107
Didn't you promise that this
would be the last time?!

00:13:29.549 --> 00:13:34.621
You said you would come back,
bringing the beginning and the end.

00:13:36.523 --> 00:13:40.927
But all you ever bring is the end.

00:13:46.633 --> 00:13:47.067
Koto!

00:13:55.008 --> 00:13:57.977
You're exactly right.

00:13:58.611 --> 00:14:02.716
All I've brought with me
today is the end.

00:14:05.719 --> 00:14:07.520
So why don't you be...

00:14:08.888 --> 00:14:10.123
...the beginning?

00:14:18.331 --> 00:14:19.833
Everyone is here!

00:14:20.867 --> 00:14:24.137
The rest is up to you, Myoue!

00:14:44.023 --> 00:14:46.025
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:14:46.025 --> 00:14:47.494
Chapter 27: The
Present (21)/ Myoue

00:15:39.546 --> 00:15:40.480
Yakushimaru!

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:41.681
Yakushimaru!

00:15:41.981 --> 00:15:42.949
Yakushimaru!

00:15:43.383 --> 00:15:44.284
Yakushimaru!

00:15:44.417 --> 00:15:45.351
Yakushimaru!

00:15:45.552 --> 00:15:46.386
Yakushimaru!

00:15:46.719 --> 00:15:48.721
Yakushimaru!

00:15:49.189 --> 00:15:50.023
Yakushimaru!

00:15:53.827 --> 00:15:54.761
Kurama...

00:15:55.195 --> 00:15:57.597
How can you sleep at a time like this?

00:15:58.231 --> 00:16:01.100
We should've ditched this idiot and ran!

00:16:01.468 --> 00:16:03.636
He can't die anyway, can he?

00:16:05.805 --> 00:16:06.406
What?

00:16:12.679 --> 00:16:16.616
Nothing you say will
make a difference at this point.

00:16:17.083 --> 00:16:19.986
What is our father thinking?

00:16:21.187 --> 00:16:23.256
Anyway, let's get out of here.

00:16:23.456 --> 00:16:26.025
If only I had my controller...

00:16:26.693 --> 00:16:28.728
Even if we can leave, then what?

00:16:30.263 --> 00:16:31.598
Does it matter anymore?

00:16:32.198 --> 00:16:33.900
What else can we do?

00:16:34.834 --> 00:16:37.871
Even if they come back,
nothing will change.

00:16:38.538 --> 00:16:40.940
It'll just get worse.

00:16:42.609 --> 00:16:44.444
Even Koto's gone crazy.

00:16:45.011 --> 00:16:45.945
Now what do we do?

00:16:46.579 --> 00:16:47.113
Myoue.

00:16:47.547 --> 00:16:51.584
It might be easier for us
if we just stay buried.

00:16:51.985 --> 00:16:52.785
Myoue!

00:16:52.785 --> 00:16:53.653
Wha—

00:16:54.354 --> 00:16:55.622
Enough.

00:16:56.022 --> 00:16:58.224
How long are you going
to sit there and sulk?

00:16:59.792 --> 00:17:01.594
Don't expect anything from others.

00:17:02.128 --> 00:17:03.630
If you don't change,

00:17:03.963 --> 00:17:06.199
your world never will.

00:17:07.133 --> 00:17:10.336
Stop brooding over a past
that's dead and gone.

00:17:14.541 --> 00:17:19.846
We are false siblings,
created to make you feel better.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:24.918
You understand, right?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.454
Myoue!

00:17:32.325 --> 00:17:36.763
You were the one who was supposed
to rule the city, Myoue.

00:17:37.764 --> 00:17:39.132
The Council of Three

00:17:39.432 --> 00:17:42.669
was simply a cradle for you
until you accepted that.

00:17:45.071 --> 00:17:49.609
You must leave
this comfortable womb...

00:17:50.843 --> 00:17:53.580
You know that, don't you?

00:17:54.714 --> 00:17:55.548
Myoue!

00:18:01.354 --> 00:18:02.488
Don't look down.

00:18:08.561 --> 00:18:10.263
Don't be afraid, Myoue.

00:18:11.097 --> 00:18:14.968
The task you must do isn't in the past.

00:18:15.969 --> 00:18:17.103
Look straight ahead.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:18.905
Go forward.

00:18:19.939 --> 00:18:20.907
Don't worry.

00:18:21.407 --> 00:18:23.710
Your past won't disappear.

00:18:24.711 --> 00:18:30.316
To long for the future doesn't
mean you betray the past,

00:18:31.117 --> 00:18:32.318
Yakushimaru.

00:18:35.521 --> 00:18:36.422
You're late.

00:18:36.656 --> 00:18:37.757
I'm sorry.

00:18:38.191 --> 00:18:42.095
But I brought all the repair
materials that were left.

00:18:42.428 --> 00:18:44.597
Okay, let's go!

00:18:44.597 --> 00:18:47.233
There's no telling when we're
going to disappear, too.

00:18:48.001 --> 00:18:49.636
See ya later, fake monk.

00:18:49.869 --> 00:18:52.238
If we don't disappear, that is.

00:18:52.472 --> 00:18:54.073
I'll go on ahead.

00:18:54.374 --> 00:18:55.775
You can do what you want.

00:18:57.844 --> 00:19:03.316
To think that, even now,
it's brighter outside than in a hole...

00:19:04.851 --> 00:19:05.885
Kind of funny.

00:19:19.699 --> 00:19:21.334
When was it, I wonder?

00:19:22.268 --> 00:19:25.104
Beneath a sunny evening sky,

00:19:25.872 --> 00:19:30.343
our boat lingered dreamily...

00:19:31.778 --> 00:19:36.182
Three children nestling near,

00:19:36.582 --> 00:19:38.751
pleased a simple tale to hear.

00:19:39.952 --> 00:19:43.956
The echoes of their laughter and
those happy memories are gone now,

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:47.694
slain by the chill autumn frost.

00:19:49.429 --> 00:19:52.432
Where has she gone,

00:19:53.132 --> 00:19:55.735
that girl who shone
beneath those skies?

00:20:06.646 --> 00:20:07.513
Yase?

00:20:08.715 --> 00:20:10.817
Look at that light!

00:20:11.517 --> 00:20:12.752
It's so pretty!

00:20:13.152 --> 00:20:14.754
Can you go get it for me?

00:20:15.722 --> 00:20:16.322
No.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.025
That's a shame.

00:20:19.258 --> 00:20:22.562
You should stop sitting there and run—

00:20:23.629 --> 00:20:25.398
Run where?

00:20:25.531 --> 00:20:26.399
It's fine.

00:20:26.766 --> 00:20:28.868
| like this place.

00:20:29.368 --> 00:20:30.636
That's why I'm here, you know.

00:20:32.338 --> 00:20:33.239
What about you?

00:20:35.541 --> 00:20:37.543
Why are you here?

00:20:40.213 --> 00:20:41.714
Just happened by.

00:20:41.714 --> 00:20:42.315
| see.

00:20:43.149 --> 00:20:46.052
But you don't mind this place, do you?

00:20:48.855 --> 00:20:49.455
Yase...

00:20:50.022 --> 00:20:54.327
You always wanted to die,

00:20:55.027 --> 00:20:59.031
but you never wanted this city to die.

00:20:59.999 --> 00:21:03.936
So while I always thought you
were a no-good little brother,

00:21:04.303 --> 00:21:07.507
| never minded you being "Myoue."

00:21:13.012 --> 00:21:17.550
In a wonderland they lie,
dreaming as the days go by.

00:21:18.718 --> 00:21:22.188
Summer dies, and all that
is left are dreams.

00:21:23.422 --> 00:21:25.424
And ever they drift down the stream,

00:21:25.925 --> 00:21:28.628
lingering in the golden gleam.

00:21:29.662 --> 00:21:34.534
Life, what is it but a dream?

00:22:08.267 --> 00:22:09.101
Thanks.

00:22:13.873 --> 00:22:15.241
Koto!

00:22:22.148 --> 00:22:24.016
You're crying again?

00:22:35.561 --> 00:22:38.664
You cry a lot more than
I'd have thought.

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:42.802
So do |, actually.

00:22:55.815 --> 00:22:56.983
Myoue...

00:22:58.251 --> 00:22:59.051
Hey.

00:22:59.485 --> 00:23:00.386
Myoue?

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.054
Myoue!

00:23:02.421 --> 00:23:03.789
Myoue, what do I do?

00:23:03.789 --> 00:23:05.791
The world's going to
end and it's my fault!

00:23:06.125 --> 00:23:07.526
No, it won't.

00:23:08.494 --> 00:23:09.795
| won't let it.

00:23:10.162 --> 00:23:10.796
Probably.

00:23:12.698 --> 00:23:15.001
When our father went away,

00:23:15.501 --> 00:23:18.104
he left us more than his promise.

00:23:19.672 --> 00:23:22.875
He also left his power of creation.

00:23:23.843 --> 00:23:24.644
Myoue...

00:23:25.745 --> 00:23:28.814
| don't want it to just end like this.

00:23:30.716 --> 00:23:33.319
I'm sorry I said you were the end.

00:23:34.921 --> 00:23:38.824
Koto, you are my beginning.

00:23:47.266 --> 00:23:53.673
I'd even cut things off, (Ouch!)
to prove the fact I exist.

00:23:55.508 --> 00:24:01.614
Though eternal lies surround me,
they're my safety line.

00:24:03.416 --> 00:24:10.022
"Wanna take you high?"
The galaxy shakes. You smile.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:18.064
I want to touch you. I don't want
to hear that it's forbidden.

00:24:19.865 --> 00:24:23.502
Moved to emotion by arguments,
| cast aside reason.

00:24:23.502 --> 00:24:28.641
I enter a game of risk that's
devoid of reason.

00:24:31.911 --> 00:24:36.682
It's resplendent with rare pain.

00:24:40.119 --> 00:24:45.191
Mistaking the real for the unreal.

00:24:48.327 --> 00:24:52.231
It transcends all understanding.

00:24:52.231 --> 00:24:53.165
So, fight!

00:24:56.435 --> 00:24:57.303
So, fight!

00:25:00.539 --> 00:25:01.374
So, fight!

00:25:08.581 --> 00:25:09.482
So, fight!

00:25:10.049 --> 00:25:12.051
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:25:12.051 --> 00:25:13.586
It was so long!

00:25:13.586 --> 00:25:14.987
It was so fun!

00:25:14.987 --> 00:25:16.622
I'm so hungry!

00:25:16.889 --> 00:25:18.591
Can I die?

00:25:18.791 --> 00:25:20.326
| want to go outside.

00:25:20.326 --> 00:25:21.427
Mom!

00:25:21.427 --> 00:25:22.828
| love you!

00:25:22.828 --> 00:25:24.363
Everyone's so lively today.

00:25:24.563 --> 00:25:25.698
Did something happen?

00:25:25.698 --> 00:25:27.433
It's the last episode, I heard.

00:25:27.433 --> 00:25:28.534
No!

00:25:28.534 --> 00:25:34.707
<i>ANen@ Nows A B, Sy Like Next time on Kyousougiga: "A
Nanga Novie About People Who Have a Fun, Busy Life!"</i>

00:25:35.041 --> 00:25:37.009
Special Move:

00:25:37.243 --> 00:25:39.145
Finale!
